Whether Congress will bow to the pressure remains to be seen. Republicans are not[ keen] on handing Democrats a shutdown to use against them in advance of the November elections,[ so] some movement is likely. However, Congress has only a handful of working days before the September 30 deadline. We would think the worthies would red[ouble] their efforts to get the budget passed, and forge a compromise the president can accept. But nothing with Congress is certain, except they can be counted on to wait until the last minute to act.[][][][][][][][][][][][][][][][][][][][]

